==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|cerebrum||brain, skull}}; see there for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɛ.ɹɪ.bɹəm/|/sɪˈɹiː.bɹəm/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cerebra|s}}

# {{lb|en|neuroanatomy}} The upper part of the brain, which is divided into the two [[cerebral]] [[hemisphere]]s. In humans it is the largest part of the brain and is the seat of [[motor]] and [[sensory]] functions, and the higher mental functions such as [[consciousness]], [[thought]], [[reason]], [[emotion]], and [[memory]].

